rules_rust fixes for the x86_64-pc-windows-gnu credential provider target.

1. `rust/platform/triple_mappings.bzl`: rules_rust deliberately omits the
   *-windows-gnu triples because they map to the same Bazel constraints
   (@platforms//os:windows + @platforms//cpu:x86_64) as *-windows-msvc, so a
   single select cannot distinguish them. This repository builds only the gnu
   variant (the Windows credential provider links with the hermetic zig
   cc_toolchain, no Visual Studio), and its crate_universe lock lists only the
   gnu triple, so declaring it is unambiguous here. Without the entry
   `@rules_rust//rust/platform:x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` does not exist and every
   generated crate select fails to resolve.
2. `rust/private/rustc.bzl`: rules_rust declares an MSVC-style
   `<name>.dll.lib` import library as an output of every Windows cdylib. On
   windows-gnu rustc writes `<name>.dll.a` instead and never the declared
   path, so the action would fail with "output was not created". The extra
   output is only meaningful for MSVC consumers, so it is gated on
   `target_abi == "msvc"`.

--- a/rust/private/rustc.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/rustc.bzl
@@ -2012 +2012 @@
-    if toolchain.target_os == "windows" and crate_info.type == "cdylib":
+    if toolchain.target_os == "windows" and toolchain.target_abi == "msvc" and crate_info.type == "cdylib":

